# 1. MEMBER 1: DATABASE DESIGN AGREEMENT & DATA POPULATION
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Report Reference: Section 3.5.1 (Table 3.5.1) & Figure 3.5 (Entity-Relationship Diagram)
# Total Tables in PostgreSQL: 17
#
# Schema Mapping Table:
# 1. users                  - PK: user_id | Base entity, role ENUM, password_hash
# 2. customers              - PK: customer_id (FK -> users) | 1:1, delivery address
# 3. vendors                - PK: vendor_id (FK -> users) | 1:1, shop_name, stall location
# 4. delivery_agents        - PK: agent_id (FK -> users) | 1:1, status, vehicle
# 5. vendor_kyc_submissions - PK: submission_id (FK -> vendors) | NIN, ID docs, stall proof
# 6. categories             - PK: category_id | 11 foodstuff categories with self-referencing FK
# 7. products               - PK: product_id (FK -> vendors, categories) | Soft-deletion (is_active)
# 8. product_images         - PK: image_id (FK -> products) | Cloudinary CDN URLs, is_primary
# 9. carts                  - PK: cart_id (FK -> customers) | 1:1 persistent container
# 10. cart_items            - PK: cart_item_id (FK -> carts, products) | Atomic qty upsert
# 11. orders                - PK: order_id (FK -> customers) | Master order, 1200 NGN fee
# 12. order_items           - PK: order_item_id (FK -> orders, products, vendors) | Frozen price snapshot
# 13. delivery_assignments  - PK: assignment_id (FK -> orders, delivery_agents) | Rider dispatch
# 14. driver_dispatch_logs  - PK: log_id (FK -> delivery_assignments) | SMS/WhatsApp/Mail logs
# 15. notifications         - PK: notification_id (FK -> users) | In-app mail records
# 16. order_disputes        - PK: dispute_id (FK -> orders, customers) | Customer grievance mediation
# 17. reviews               - PK: review_id (FK -> products, customers) | 1-5 star ratings & feedback
#
# Data Population Proofs:
# - User Registration Form   -> authController.js (bcrypt 12 rounds, inserts into users + customers/vendors)
# - Vendor KYC Form          -> kycController.js (populates vendor_kyc_submissions with drag & drop files; auto-links bank details from onboarding)
# - Product Upload Form      -> productController.js (populates products and product_images)
# - Checkout Form            -> orderModel.createOrderFromCart (atomic transaction into orders & order_items)

