# 3. MEMBER 3: SOFTWARE ARCHITECTURE, DESIGN PATTERNS & CODE INSPECTION
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Report Reference: Section 3.2 (Agile Scrum), Section 3.4 (UML), Section 3.5 (OOAM)
#
# High-Level Architecture:
# - Presentation Layer: React 19 SPA, Tailwind CSS v4, Context API (Auth, Cart, Wishlist)
# - Application Layer: Node.js + Express.js REST API (Controller-Service-Model)
# - Database Layer: PostgreSQL 14+ Connection Pool (pg.Pool) with ACID Transactions
#
# Core Unit Modules (Functions) to Inspect:
# 1. authenticate & authorize (Backend/src/middleware/auth.js):
#    Stateless JWT verification (24h expiry per NFR02) and Role-Based Access Control.
# 2. requireVerifiedVendor (Backend/src/middleware/auth.js):
#    DB-backed security check preventing unvetted vendors from listing/editing products.
# 3. computeCartTotal (Backend/src/models/orderModel.js):
#    Server-side price verification; never trusts client-supplied sums.
# 4. updateOrderStatus (Backend/src/models/orderModel.js):
#    Status state machine using explicit PostgreSQL type cast ($2::varchar) for reliable execution.
#
# Integrated System Modules to Inspect:
# 1. Checkout-to-Fulfillment Pipeline (Figure 3.3 Sequence Diagram & Figure 3.4 Activity Diagram):
#    Atomic transaction (BEGIN -> stock check -> master order -> frozen line items -> agent assign -> COMMIT).
# 2. Asynchronous Notification & Mail Subsystem (FR12 / Section 2.2.2):
#    Full 3-pane client (MailPage.jsx) linked to live triggers (Order placed, KYC approved, dispatch).
